  "reasoning": "The patient reports stiffness and weakness in the neck muscles, enlarged joints ('joints have grown'), and extreme discomfort when walking due to stiffness. These symptoms directly match the clinical presentation of arthritis, particularly joint swelling and mobility impairment. Reference [1] contains an almost identical symptom description and confirms the diagnosis as arthritis. Cervical spondylosis was considered due to the neck stiffness, but it is factually ruled out because the patient lacks its defining characteristics (back pain, dry cough, stiffness in the arms and legs, balance problems, and dizziness). The explicit mention of enlarged joints and walking difficulty firmly establishes arthritis over cervical spondylosis.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]arthritis[/DIAGNOSIS]"
